To create a Chrome extension that saves the contents of the current webpage, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Set up your project structure.
2. Create the necessary files for the extension (manifest.json, background.js, content.js).
3. Write code in each file to handle saving the webpage's content.

Here is an example of how you can set this up:

**Project Structure:**
```
webpage-saver/
│
├── manifest.json
├── background.js
└── content.js
```

**manifest.json:**
```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Webpage Saver",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Saves the contents of the current webpage.",
  "permissions": ["activeTab", "storage"],
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_icon": {
      "16": "icons/icon16.png",
      "48": "icons/icon48.png",
      "128": "icons/icon128.png"
    }
  },
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"]
    }
  ]
}
```

**background.js:**
```javascript
chrome.action.onClicked.addListener((tab) => {
  chrome.scripting.executeScript({
    target: { tabId: tab.id },
    files: ['content.js']
  });
});
```

**content.js:**
```javascript
// Get the title and URL of the current page
const pageTitle = document.title;
const pageUrl = window.location.href;

// Save the HTML content of the page
const pageContent = document.documentElement.outerHTML;

// Send the data back to the background script
chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ type: 'savePage', data: { title: pageTitle, url: pageUrl, content: pageContent } }, (response) => {
  console.log('Page saved:', response);
});
```

This setup will allow users to click on the browser action icon, which triggers the `content.js` script to run on the active tab. The script then collects the title, URL, and HTML content of the page and sends it back to the background script via `chrome.runtime.sendMessage`. You would typically store this information locally or send it to a server depending on your requirements.

Remember to replace `"icons/icon16.png"`, `"icons/icon48.png"`, and `"icons/icon128.png"` with actual paths to your icons if they exist. Also, ensure that you have appropriate permissions and security measures in place when handling user data.

