Sure! An impossible triangle, also known as the Penrose triangle or tribar, is a geometric figure that appears to be a solid object but cannot exist in three-dimensional space without self-intersection.

Here's how you can create an impossible triangle using SVG (Scalable Vector Graphics) and add some 3D effects:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Impossible Triangle</title>
    <style>
        body {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
        }
        svg {
            width: 200px;
            height: 200px;
            transform-style: preserve-3d;
            animation: rotate 5s infinite linear;
        }
        @keyframes rotate {
            from { transform: rotateY(0deg); }
            to { transform: rotateY(360deg); }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <svg viewBox="-100 -100 200 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <!-- Front face -->
        <polygon points="-50,-50 50,-50 0,50" fill="#ffcccb" stroke="#990000" stroke-width="2"/>

        <!-- Back face -->
        <polygon points="50,-50 -50,-50 0,50" fill="#add8e6" stroke="#0000ff" stroke-width="2" transform="translate(0,0) scale(1,-1)"/>

        <!-- Left side -->
        <polygon points="-50,-50 0,50 0,-50" fill="#90ee90" stroke="#006400" stroke-width="2" transform="rotate(-90,0,0) translate(0,0) scale(1,-1)"/>

        <!-- Right side -->
        <polygon points="50,-50 0,50 0,-50" fill="#ffd700" stroke="#ff8c00" stroke-width="2" transform="rotate(90,0,0) translate(0,0) scale(1,-1)"/>
    </svg>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **SVG Structure**: The `<svg>` element defines the canvas for our drawing.
2. **ViewBox**: Sets up the coordinate system where `-100,-100` is at the top-left corner and `200,200` is at the bottom-right corner.
3. **Polygons**:
   - Each polygon represents one of the faces of the impossible triangle.
   - They use different colors and transformations (`transform`) to simulate depth and rotation.
4. **Transformations**:
   - `scale(1,-1)` flips the polygons vertically to give them a 3D appearance.
   - `rotate()` rotates each polygon around its axis to form the illusion of a 3D structure.
5. **Animation**: A simple CSS animation rotates the entire SVG element continuously to enhance the 3D effect.

This code creates a basic version of an impossible triangle with animated rotation. You can further customize the colors, sizes, and animations to suit your needs.

